ok - teleport refuses a dirty or already-occupied remote before touching the worker
ok - a failed teleport leaves the local task intact and runnable
ok - pack snapshots tracked and untracked work under refs/teleport/<task> without moving the worker
ok - teleport out moves work, records, transcript, and backlog item to the remote and cleans up here
ok - teleport --back reverses the move
ok - a non-Claude task relaunches from its brief plus a generated progress note
ok - a Claude task without a transcript falls back to brief plus progress note
ok - a failed backlog handoff after takeover warns instead of rolling the remote back
ok - an early backlog handoff failure holds the local item instead of leaving it dispatchable
ok - a round trip replaces the earlier teleport note
ok - no teleport, out or back, pushes anything to the project's origin
ok - an adopting clone behind origin fetches the snapshot's history before installing it
ok - teleport refuses mid-validation
ok - abort refuses a task this home did not adopt
ok - remind raises one rate-limited notification only while workers run
ok - fm-spawn refuses --teleport with relaunch, secondmate, or batch spawns
ok - fm-spawn --teleport resumes the Claude session with the arrival note as its launch record, before its backlog item arrives
